# Every file is checked out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# This is not a style preference. `corpus_sha256` in a results file is an
# integrity claim -- "these exact bytes produced these exact numbers" -- and a
# checkout that rewrites line endings makes the same corpus hash differently on
# Windows and on Linux, which turns the claim into a statement about the
# operating system. Pinning the endings is what makes the digest mean anything.
* text=auto eol=lf
